    "body": "I think if the input display `current length vs max length` such as `15/30` would be great. Both users see how many left they can type, and how many characters they've inputed. Kill 2 birds with 1 stone.\n\nIf the soft enforcement is allowed, who will handle validation of form submission when input exceeds the max length?\n\nP.S. this could be hard when accept a new line character since Windows and Unix use different character (CRLF vs LF) so the count are different, so as to number of character user type.",
